 "title": "Methylation and Cardiovascular Disease Connections",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the connections between methylation processes, cardiovascular disease (CVD), and various organisms. Hcy and SAH, chemicals associated with CVD, accumulate in Drosophila and yeast, indicating their involvement in these organisms. SAHH, a gene or protein, causes growth defects in Drosophila and yeast, while its deletion in yeast suggests its importance. Histone methylation, catalyzed by Dot1, is inhibited by Hcy and SAH, highlighting the interplay between methylation and CVD-related chemicals. The cluster also includes various methods and tools, such as Western blot analysis, Polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis, and NMR, used in the analysis of these organisms and processes.",
